\active makes the editor pane it is executed in active.
It takes no arguments:

\active

Its counterpart is \inactive. When a pane is inactive,
executing lines in it does nothing, except for a line that
contains only \active (without any indentation or other
text), which makes the pane active again.
Panes are active by default.

This is useful to prevent code in a pane from being
executed by accident.
